1
00:00:15,610 --> 00:00:17,130
What should I do?

2
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:19,470
I’m worried about Grandma.

3
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:21,830
Why is my luck so terrible?

4
00:00:32,490 --> 00:00:34,870
This year, you’ll enter a new social circle,

5
00:00:36,340 --> 00:00:38,870
where you’ll inevitably face conflict

6
00:00:39,690 --> 00:00:41,890
because you aren’t accepted.

7
00:00:41,890 --> 00:00:45,670
And earning acceptance there won’t be easy.

8
00:00:46,430 --> 00:00:48,740
You have to learn how to survive

9
00:00:49,910 --> 00:00:53,210
and prove yourself with your abilities.

10
00:00:54,430 --> 00:00:54,980
Oh.

11
00:00:57,210 --> 00:00:59,870
A foreigner will bring trouble into your life.

12
00:02:24,360 --> 00:02:25,079
Ah!

13
00:02:27,030 --> 00:02:29,460
Great, why is your dream so vivid?

14
00:02:29,990 --> 00:02:32,790
Wake up already. Wake up, Great!

15
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:37,550
Whose body is this?

16
00:02:37,960 --> 00:02:39,350
Stop! Where are you going?

17
00:02:39,510 --> 00:02:40,220
To the toilet.

18
00:02:40,420 --> 00:02:42,180
What’s a toilet, and what do you do there?

19
00:02:42,610 --> 00:02:43,329
To take a dump.

20
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:44,530
Hey, Gaew.

21
00:02:46,670 --> 00:02:48,720
This Gaew doesn’t seem like the old Gaew.

22
00:02:48,980 --> 00:02:50,250
Come on, strike me!

23
00:02:50,250 --> 00:02:51,530
What are you doing, Gaew?

24
00:02:52,610 --> 00:02:53,920
I want lightning to strike me,

25
00:02:54,340 --> 00:02:55,850
so I can go back to where I came from.

26
00:02:58,640 --> 00:03:02,420
(Bangkok, 2026)

27
00:03:23,810 --> 00:03:26,140
Rich, you have to help him.

28
00:03:31,640 --> 00:03:33,190
No matter what’s wrong with Great,

29
00:03:33,190 --> 00:03:34,579
or how hard it is.

30
00:03:36,579 --> 00:03:38,579
Even if I have to sell my resort,

31
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:40,210
I’ll do it.

32
00:03:42,640 --> 00:03:43,660
Yes, Grandma.

33
00:04:00,100 --> 00:04:02,880
(Year 1036 of Thai minor era)

34
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:06,480
Why do you think Gaew did it?

35
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:07,700
I didn’t do it, P’Sri.

36
00:04:08,570 --> 00:04:09,960
This is my first time meeting Bua.

37
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:11,900
How could I get her pregnant?

38
00:04:12,320 --> 00:04:13,300
Lies.

39
00:04:13,300 --> 00:04:16,610
I know people like you always lie.

40
00:04:16,610 --> 00:04:18,700
Stop making excuses.

41
00:04:18,700 --> 00:04:21,860
A troublemaker like you

42
00:04:21,860 --> 00:04:24,790
is bound to do something like this.

43
00:04:24,790 --> 00:04:27,990
I’m not surprised you did this to Bua.

44
00:04:30,550 --> 00:04:31,820
Dear.

45
00:04:33,210 --> 00:04:34,610
I’m sorry

46
00:04:35,170 --> 00:04:37,390
for not raising Gaew properly.

47
00:04:37,390 --> 00:04:40,720
I tried to love and raise him

48
00:04:40,720 --> 00:04:43,210
the same way I raised Sri and Dech.

49
00:04:44,210 --> 00:04:47,440
But I don’t know why he can’t be good

50
00:04:47,440 --> 00:04:50,280
and always brings us trouble.

51
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:54,460
It’s my fault.

52
00:04:55,680 --> 00:04:57,210
The doctor told us that

53
00:04:57,500 --> 00:05:00,920
Bua is already two months pregnant.

54
00:05:00,920 --> 00:05:04,100
If this child is Gaew’s,

55
00:05:04,100 --> 00:05:05,660
then that means

56
00:05:06,190 --> 00:05:10,340
it’s the grandchild of Lord Ramnarong, your friend.

57
00:05:10,700 --> 00:05:11,860
This is ridiculous.

58
00:05:12,880 --> 00:05:14,570
I met Bua for the first time today.

59
00:05:15,100 --> 00:05:16,340
How could I get her pregnant?

60
00:05:16,550 --> 00:05:18,120
Enough with the excuses.

61
00:05:18,720 --> 00:05:20,920
Bua lives here.

62
00:05:21,590 --> 00:05:23,920
What do you mean it's your first meeting?

63
00:05:23,920 --> 00:05:25,120
I’m telling the truth.

64
00:05:25,120 --> 00:05:26,140
Are you talking back?

65
00:05:26,140 --> 00:05:27,170
Mother.

66
00:05:28,860 --> 00:05:31,150
May I ask Bua a few questions?

67
00:05:31,150 --> 00:05:33,060
What else do you need to ask her?

68
00:05:33,060 --> 00:05:36,500
-I’ve already asked everything.
-Please let me.

69
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:38,500
Jumpa.

70
00:05:39,460 --> 00:05:41,700
Just let Sri ask.

71
00:05:42,500 --> 00:05:45,040
So we’ll get the full story.

72
00:05:50,570 --> 00:05:51,390
Bua.

73
00:05:52,350 --> 00:05:53,880
Let me ask you again.

74
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:56,520
Who got you pregnant?

75
00:06:15,590 --> 00:06:17,880
-Where are you going?
-Shh.

76
00:06:21,990 --> 00:06:23,610
Answer me.

77
00:06:23,610 --> 00:06:25,260
It was Lord Gaew.

78
00:06:25,420 --> 00:06:26,920
Then tell me.

79
00:06:27,240 --> 00:06:29,720
When did Gaew do that to you?

80
00:06:34,320 --> 00:06:36,040
That’s enough, Sri.

81
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:38,840
She’s been hurt enough.

82
00:06:43,100 --> 00:06:45,659
Something improper happened in our household.

83
00:06:45,659 --> 00:06:47,900
And Gaew claimed he’s accused.

84
00:06:47,900 --> 00:06:50,100
When both sides are telling different stories,

85
00:06:50,100 --> 00:06:52,140
I can’t let it slide.

86
00:06:53,659 --> 00:06:55,409
I agree with P’Sri, Mother.

87
00:06:58,409 --> 00:07:00,210
Answer me, Bua.

88
00:07:05,790 --> 00:07:07,410
It happened last month.

89
00:07:07,410 --> 00:07:09,220
You said you’re two months pregnant.

90
00:07:10,040 --> 00:07:12,100
So how could it be last month?

91
00:07:19,640 --> 00:07:21,500
And how did you know you’re pregnant?

92
00:07:23,500 --> 00:07:25,500
How did I know?

93
00:07:26,720 --> 00:07:29,060
Why would you ask such a question?

94
00:07:29,440 --> 00:07:32,060
How could a woman not know she’s pregnant?

95
00:07:34,860 --> 00:07:37,260
Just tell him you’ve been feeling dizzy,

96
00:07:37,260 --> 00:07:39,500
having headaches, and feeling unwell.

97
00:07:40,320 --> 00:07:41,640
Yes.

98
00:07:41,640 --> 00:07:44,610
I’ve been dizzy and nauseous,

99
00:07:44,610 --> 00:07:46,300
and feeling unwell.

100
00:07:46,640 --> 00:07:48,100
Then how did you two do it?

101
00:07:49,750 --> 00:07:51,210
Did Gaew force himself on you?

102
00:07:55,120 --> 00:07:56,190
Is that true, Gaew?

103
00:07:58,320 --> 00:07:59,700
Who examined you?

104
00:08:02,770 --> 00:08:05,080
There was no doctor, was there?

105
00:08:09,320 --> 00:08:10,480
Since it’s come to this,

106
00:08:11,010 --> 00:08:12,440
then I’ll examine Bua…

107
00:08:12,790 --> 00:08:14,180
and see if she’s really pregnant.

108
00:08:16,520 --> 00:08:17,680
Are you a doctor?

109
00:08:19,100 --> 00:08:20,210
How can you examine her?

110
00:08:24,750 --> 00:08:25,820
Please let me try.

111
00:08:30,770 --> 00:08:32,990
Bua, give me your hand.

112
00:08:44,320 --> 00:08:45,810
Come on, Bua.

113
00:08:57,570 --> 00:08:58,860
So strange.

114
00:08:59,860 --> 00:09:01,170
If you’re really pregnant,

115
00:09:01,590 --> 00:09:02,820
what are you afraid of?

116
00:09:07,100 --> 00:09:09,370
Are you making excuses now?

117
00:09:09,880 --> 00:09:11,550
What are you going to do with Bua?

118
00:09:12,410 --> 00:09:13,550
Auntie.

119
00:09:14,280 --> 00:09:15,920
What could I possibly do?

120
00:09:19,080 --> 00:09:20,390
She still has her period.

121
00:09:27,060 --> 00:09:27,810
Bua.

122
00:09:29,660 --> 00:09:31,660
You still have your period, haven’t you?

123
00:09:36,570 --> 00:09:38,410
Am I right?

124
00:09:46,480 --> 00:09:48,610
That’s a betel juice stain.

125
00:09:50,980 --> 00:09:52,980
Betel juice stain?

126
00:09:53,900 --> 00:09:55,300
Are you sure?

127
00:09:59,880 --> 00:10:02,120
Bua, this cloth belongs to you, doesn’t it?

128
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:07,560
Yes.

129
00:10:08,440 --> 00:10:11,440
Why do you still have your period if you’re pregnant?

130
00:10:16,640 --> 00:10:17,460
Hm?

131
00:10:23,750 --> 00:10:26,150
A lie has no legs.

132
00:10:27,480 --> 00:10:28,500
That’s true.

133
00:10:29,920 --> 00:10:32,180
Sri, are you saying I’m lying?

134
00:10:37,520 --> 00:10:39,210
I was talking about Bua.

135
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:42,210
Not you, mother.

136
00:10:43,770 --> 00:10:46,180
Why are you getting defensive?

137
00:10:47,190 --> 00:10:49,010
I’m not defensive.

138
00:10:49,010 --> 00:10:50,420
I’m perfectly normal.

139
00:10:58,370 --> 00:11:00,320
Let’s do this.

140
00:11:01,520 --> 00:11:03,700
If you refuse to tell the truth,

141
00:11:03,700 --> 00:11:06,260
I’ll hand you over to the authorities for questioning.

142
00:11:07,770 --> 00:11:11,440
And you’ll be whipped until you confess.

143
00:11:15,370 --> 00:11:16,840
I lied.

144
00:11:16,840 --> 00:11:18,320
I’m not pregnant.

145
00:11:18,320 --> 00:11:20,170
I was only following orders.

146
00:11:21,240 --> 00:11:23,720
You’re lying. My lady never ordered you.

147
00:11:23,720 --> 00:11:25,060
But Aunt Prik did.

148
00:11:25,060 --> 00:11:26,260
Prik!

149
00:11:35,150 --> 00:11:36,300
Fine.

150
00:11:36,790 --> 00:11:38,260
I admit it.

151
00:11:38,860 --> 00:11:40,770
I was the one who ordered Prik.

152
00:11:41,280 --> 00:11:43,770
And Prik ordered Bua to do it.

153
00:11:53,420 --> 00:11:55,120
I did all this

154
00:11:55,750 --> 00:11:57,810
to protect our family.

155
00:11:58,840 --> 00:12:01,660
I don’t want Gaew to stay here.

156
00:12:02,260 --> 00:12:05,550
Because he only brings disgrace upon us.

157
00:12:09,660 --> 00:12:10,900
Jumpa.

158
00:12:11,390 --> 00:12:13,100
Even so,

159
00:12:13,390 --> 00:12:17,100
lying is still wrong.

160
00:12:18,640 --> 00:12:19,750
A sin is a sin,

161
00:12:20,280 --> 00:12:22,010
no matter who commits it.

162
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:25,350
The day before,

163
00:12:25,660 --> 00:12:27,350
Gaew’s already apologized

164
00:12:27,350 --> 00:12:29,460
and promised to turn over a new leaf, didn’t he?

165
00:12:29,460 --> 00:12:32,610
Why do you have to drag up the past

166
00:12:33,210 --> 00:12:34,990
and make up lies?

167
00:12:36,700 --> 00:12:38,080
I understand now.

168
00:12:46,860 --> 00:12:47,610
Mother.

169
00:12:50,440 --> 00:12:52,190
I brought a gift for you.

170
00:12:55,440 --> 00:12:56,380
What is it?

171
00:13:17,840 --> 00:13:19,720
Durian stinks so bad.

172
00:13:20,240 --> 00:13:21,980
Take it away.

173
00:13:26,570 --> 00:13:27,880
I feel you, Dech.

174
00:13:28,300 --> 00:13:29,880
Sri.

175
00:13:29,880 --> 00:13:32,100
You said you brought me a gift,

176
00:13:32,100 --> 00:13:34,920
but this is more like a gift for your father.

177
00:13:35,700 --> 00:13:36,920
You have a point.

178
00:13:39,260 --> 00:13:41,390
-Would you like some, my lady?
-Prik.

179
00:13:41,700 --> 00:13:43,220
Take it away from me.

180
00:13:43,220 --> 00:13:45,970
Take it wherever you want.

181
00:13:45,970 --> 00:13:47,220
I’m serious.

182
00:14:26,390 --> 00:14:27,750
Look at you.

183
00:14:29,080 --> 00:14:32,240
I forgot you two don’t like durian.

184
00:14:32,880 --> 00:14:36,700
But something this good doesn’t come around every day.

185
00:14:37,080 --> 00:14:37,840
Exactly.

186
00:14:38,370 --> 00:14:39,610
I don’t think it smells bad.

187
00:14:40,350 --> 00:14:42,460
It smells really good.

188
00:14:43,100 --> 00:14:46,460
Oh, look at you.

189
00:14:47,520 --> 00:14:50,520
Durian is the king of fruits.

190
00:14:51,120 --> 00:14:52,550
Something this good,

191
00:14:52,940 --> 00:14:54,300
why don’t you enjoy it?

192
00:15:06,720 --> 00:15:07,860
Excuse me.

193
00:15:15,970 --> 00:15:16,840
Gaew.

194
00:15:18,680 --> 00:15:20,020
Thank you so much, P’Sri.

195
00:15:20,750 --> 00:15:23,810
I would’ve ended up being the scapegoat without you.

196
00:15:25,280 --> 00:15:26,970
Don’t say that, Gaew.

197
00:15:27,810 --> 00:15:29,440
I only did the right thing.

198
00:15:29,790 --> 00:15:32,300
The truth always comes out in the end.

199
00:15:44,920 --> 00:15:46,840
Don’t be angry with my mother.

200
00:15:48,810 --> 00:15:50,900
She’s like a fire.

201
00:15:50,900 --> 00:15:53,500
Burns hot at first, but eventually cools down.

202
00:15:54,170 --> 00:15:55,660
Don’t hold it against her.

203
00:15:58,750 --> 00:16:01,350
I didn’t mean to hurt you.

204
00:16:01,920 --> 00:16:03,100
I’m not angry.

205
00:16:04,970 --> 00:16:06,410
I understand her.

206
00:16:07,320 --> 00:16:10,460
I’m just getting a headache.

207
00:16:14,700 --> 00:16:15,580
Gaew.

208
00:16:18,040 --> 00:16:20,950
I’ve been wondering since I came back.

209
00:16:22,240 --> 00:16:25,970
Why do you speak and act differently?

210
00:16:27,100 --> 00:16:28,810
Unlike the old Gaew.

211
00:16:36,240 --> 00:16:37,210
Prik.

212
00:16:37,550 --> 00:16:38,260
Yes?

213
00:16:38,520 --> 00:16:42,810
Tell Juang to throw away those unripe durians.

214
00:16:42,810 --> 00:16:45,680
Get them out of my house right now!

215
00:16:45,680 --> 00:16:46,920
Yes, my lady.

216
00:16:48,460 --> 00:16:49,150
Wait.

217
00:16:49,810 --> 00:16:51,360
Please don’t throw them away.

218
00:16:51,360 --> 00:16:52,170
I’ll take them.

219
00:16:53,150 --> 00:16:54,280
How foolish.

220
00:16:55,190 --> 00:16:57,190
Who eat unripe durian?

221
00:16:57,810 --> 00:17:00,880
What could you possibly do with it?

222
00:17:01,210 --> 00:17:02,460
It’s edible.

223
00:17:02,810 --> 00:17:06,970
I’ll make it so those who can’t stand durian like you two,

224
00:17:06,970 --> 00:17:08,569
can eat it without any problem.

225
00:17:09,319 --> 00:17:12,339
You must be the only person in Ayutthaya

226
00:17:13,119 --> 00:17:14,839
who’s crazy enough to eat it.

227
00:17:16,040 --> 00:17:19,550
How are you going to make unripe durian edible?

228
00:17:21,170 --> 00:17:22,790
I’m curious too.

229
00:17:22,790 --> 00:17:26,140
What secret technique do you have?

230
00:17:26,520 --> 00:17:29,170
Just wait and see.

231
00:17:29,170 --> 00:17:31,640
P’Juang, P’Waen, please carry them to the kitchen.

232
00:17:31,640 --> 00:17:32,520
Yes.

233
00:17:33,410 --> 00:17:34,570
Unripe durian?

234
00:17:46,500 --> 00:17:48,460
Honestly, Sri.

235
00:17:48,840 --> 00:17:53,980
Why did you pick both the ripe and unripe ones?

236
00:17:54,610 --> 00:17:56,180
They told me I could pick,

237
00:17:57,100 --> 00:17:58,460
so I picked the tree clean.

238
00:18:09,900 --> 00:18:11,900
Coming through.

239
00:19:34,500 --> 00:19:37,440
Is this really durian?

240
00:19:38,120 --> 00:19:39,190
Yes.

241
00:19:39,620 --> 00:19:42,790
This is unripe durian fried until crispy.

242
00:19:42,790 --> 00:19:43,860
It doesn’t smell

243
00:19:44,410 --> 00:19:45,940
and can be stored for a long time.

244
00:19:51,610 --> 00:19:53,020
It’s real.

245
00:19:53,590 --> 00:19:55,020
What do you mean, Dech?

246
00:19:55,950 --> 00:19:57,100
Beautiful color.

247
00:20:01,770 --> 00:20:03,320
And it hardly smells.

248
00:20:04,880 --> 00:20:05,920
It looks delicious.

249
00:20:11,210 --> 00:20:12,560
If you want it to taste better,

250
00:20:14,040 --> 00:20:15,210
sprinkle salt on it.

251
00:20:33,260 --> 00:20:34,460
P’Sri, try it.

252
00:20:54,210 --> 00:20:57,170
Even from Lanna to Malacca,

253
00:20:57,170 --> 00:20:59,860
and from Champa to Dawei,

254
00:20:59,860 --> 00:21:04,940
I never tasted anything like this before.

255
00:21:04,940 --> 00:21:09,210
I feel strangely light and dreamy.

256
00:21:09,210 --> 00:21:11,860
Tell me.

257
00:21:11,860 --> 00:21:15,410
This is not a dream, right?

258
00:21:24,950 --> 00:21:26,460
Help.

259
00:21:26,460 --> 00:21:28,990
Someone help me.

260
00:21:28,990 --> 00:21:32,260
I can’t stop eating.

261
00:21:32,260 --> 00:21:36,660
Now I can die in peace.

262
00:21:39,150 --> 00:21:42,260
I’m afraid to swallow,

263
00:21:42,260 --> 00:21:44,860
because I don’t want it to be gone.

264
00:21:45,860 --> 00:21:47,800
Do you feel the same way?

265
00:21:49,440 --> 00:21:51,300
I’m just like you.

266
00:21:51,300 --> 00:21:55,210
I nearly cried swallowing the last bite.

267
00:21:55,210 --> 00:21:58,390
But the flavor still lingers in my mouth.

268
00:21:58,390 --> 00:22:01,760
It tastes heavenly.

269
00:22:11,320 --> 00:22:12,810
Very crunchy,

270
00:22:13,610 --> 00:22:16,640
and so perfectly crisp,

271
00:22:17,750 --> 00:22:22,410
Soft and smooth, a tasty treat,

272
00:22:23,100 --> 00:22:28,370
Every chew makes joy complete,

273
00:22:29,410 --> 00:22:34,700
Durian’s bliss is hard to beat.

274
00:22:59,020 --> 00:23:00,760
Jumpa.

275
00:23:08,840 --> 00:23:09,990
It’s really crispy

276
00:23:11,010 --> 00:23:16,280
like I'm eating an entire durian orchard.

277
00:23:16,990 --> 00:23:21,060
If this is a dream, I never want to wake up.

278
00:23:21,700 --> 00:23:23,720
But if this is real,

279
00:23:23,720 --> 00:23:28,150
why does it feel like I’m ascending to heaven?

280
00:23:28,580 --> 00:23:30,770
Gaew is amazing.

281
00:23:31,210 --> 00:23:33,900
Am I about to reach nirvana?

282
00:23:50,960 --> 00:23:52,590
What is this?

283
00:23:52,590 --> 00:23:54,300
Is this really fried durian?

284
00:23:54,700 --> 00:23:58,720
How did I live without it before?

285
00:24:03,570 --> 00:24:05,970
The flavor is extraordinary.

286
00:24:06,370 --> 00:24:08,770
Fried durian!

287
00:24:16,660 --> 00:24:18,370
Not bad, right, Dech?

288
00:24:23,770 --> 00:24:25,240
Not bad at all, P'Sri.

289
00:24:33,880 --> 00:24:35,120
I’ve changed my mind.

290
00:24:35,970 --> 00:24:36,970
It’s just so-so.

291
00:24:40,410 --> 00:24:41,370
Right, mother?

292
00:24:41,970 --> 00:24:43,500
I agree.

293
00:24:44,520 --> 00:24:46,990
Just don’t make it too often.

294
00:25:02,100 --> 00:25:02,970
Dech.

295
00:25:03,680 --> 00:25:05,460
Where’s Gaew?

296
00:25:07,590 --> 00:25:10,750
He went down to the kitchen, not sure why.

297
00:25:18,210 --> 00:25:19,300
P’Sri.

298
00:25:19,300 --> 00:25:19,860
Hm?

299
00:25:19,860 --> 00:25:23,300
Do you think Gaew has changed?

300
00:25:24,010 --> 00:25:24,970
Yes.

301
00:25:26,350 --> 00:25:27,550
What happened?

302
00:25:30,460 --> 00:25:32,160
There was a misunderstanding,

303
00:25:32,610 --> 00:25:35,100
so I used the Krishna Kali spell

304
00:25:35,920 --> 00:25:37,100
to uncover the truth.

305
00:25:41,990 --> 00:25:44,060
It must be serious

306
00:25:44,390 --> 00:25:46,550
so you resort to that spell.

307
00:25:49,480 --> 00:25:50,720
But in the end,

308
00:25:52,010 --> 00:25:53,840
Gaew hadn’t done anything evil,

309
00:25:54,590 --> 00:25:57,700
so the spell couldn’t harm him.

310
00:25:59,840 --> 00:26:00,700
No wonder.

311
00:26:01,300 --> 00:26:02,350
He’s so strange.

312
00:26:03,550 --> 00:26:04,440
He’s insane.

313
00:26:07,170 --> 00:26:09,680
What’s the Krishna Kali spell, P’Muen?

314
00:26:17,410 --> 00:26:18,120
Uh…

315
00:26:19,680 --> 00:26:21,350
it’s a prayer chant.

316
00:26:22,380 --> 00:26:23,860
You weren’t feeling well before,

317
00:26:24,610 --> 00:26:25,860
so I prayed for you.

318
00:26:27,680 --> 00:26:29,210
What kind of prayer

319
00:26:30,380 --> 00:26:32,860
sends me across centuries?

320
00:26:36,720 --> 00:26:37,770
What did you say?

321
00:26:38,750 --> 00:26:39,460
Nothing.

322
00:26:40,990 --> 00:26:42,210
I was wondering.

323
00:26:43,880 --> 00:26:44,950
Everyone...

324
00:26:45,770 --> 00:26:47,260
keeps saying I’ve changed.

325
00:26:47,920 --> 00:26:49,460
That I’m possessed.

326
00:26:50,300 --> 00:26:51,500
And you.

327
00:26:52,550 --> 00:26:54,500
You said I lost my mind.

328
00:26:55,060 --> 00:26:55,950
Didn’t you?

329
00:26:57,610 --> 00:26:59,320
You speak strangely.

330
00:26:59,900 --> 00:27:01,480
Nothing like a normal person.

331
00:27:03,570 --> 00:27:04,810
I agree with Dech.

332
00:27:05,370 --> 00:27:07,920
Maybe this is you guys' fate.

333
00:27:10,320 --> 00:27:13,390
I just hope it’s a good kind of fate.

334
00:27:15,520 --> 00:27:16,920
I think it’s a bad one.

335
00:27:17,550 --> 00:27:19,920
Maybe a doomed fate.

336
00:27:23,900 --> 00:27:24,720
There, there.

337
00:27:25,260 --> 00:27:29,260
By the way, what did you tell Pin and Yam to fetch?

338
00:27:30,500 --> 00:27:31,660
Crispy catfish salad.

339
00:27:33,190 --> 00:27:34,680
It’s really good with a drink.

340
00:27:44,970 --> 00:27:45,660
Catfish?

341
00:27:46,180 --> 00:27:47,170
Why crispy?

342
00:27:48,180 --> 00:27:49,240
How did you make it?

343
00:27:50,720 --> 00:27:52,550
It’s not that hard.

344
00:28:34,770 --> 00:28:36,320
This is another strange thing.

345
00:28:38,100 --> 00:28:40,100
Gaew never used the kitchen.

346
00:29:00,260 --> 00:29:04,750
Gaew’s spicy salad scents the air,

347
00:29:06,320 --> 00:29:10,480
Crispy catfish so light and rare,

348
00:29:11,150 --> 00:29:15,480
Tangy, fiery, rich delight,

349
00:29:17,300 --> 00:29:22,660
Melts in your mouth till the final bite.

350
00:29:25,990 --> 00:29:26,810
P’Sri.

351
00:29:27,680 --> 00:29:28,750
What got into you?

352
00:29:30,460 --> 00:29:31,320
Try it.

353
00:29:46,260 --> 00:29:47,240
Dip it in the sauce.

354
00:30:05,610 --> 00:30:08,610
It's crunchy and has many layers.

355
00:30:09,640 --> 00:30:12,950
Since when can he cook this good?

356
00:30:20,380 --> 00:30:23,370
Who exactly is this Gaew?

357
00:30:29,570 --> 00:30:32,280
Well?

358
00:30:33,680 --> 00:30:34,700
It’s average.

359
00:30:35,010 --> 00:30:36,040
Oh.

360
00:30:41,060 --> 00:30:42,480
You two brothers

361
00:30:43,460 --> 00:30:45,590
couldn’t be more different.

362
00:30:47,170 --> 00:30:49,150
One is polite,

363
00:30:49,880 --> 00:30:51,100
calm,

364
00:30:51,950 --> 00:30:53,190
kind-hearted,

365
00:30:53,990 --> 00:30:55,350
and quick-witted.

366
00:30:57,300 --> 00:30:58,440
While the other one

367
00:31:00,150 --> 00:31:01,260
is a poser,

368
00:31:02,350 --> 00:31:03,260
strict,

369
00:31:04,040 --> 00:31:05,320
and full of himself.

370
00:31:05,740 --> 00:31:07,740
You’re talking strangely again.

371
00:31:08,570 --> 00:31:10,120
You don’t know me well.

372
00:31:10,590 --> 00:31:12,350
You don’t know me well either, P'Muen.

373
00:31:13,190 --> 00:31:15,260
Lord Gaew really has changed a lot.

374
00:31:15,260 --> 00:31:18,610
He’s become considerate and caring.

375
00:31:18,610 --> 00:31:20,340
Even so,

376
00:31:20,340 --> 00:31:22,970
that doesn’t compare to Lord Muen’s perfection.

377
00:31:23,610 --> 00:31:24,900
He’s handsome,

378
00:31:25,590 --> 00:31:26,920
composed,

379
00:31:27,720 --> 00:31:29,340
and talented.

380
00:31:29,770 --> 00:31:32,080
His reputation spreads throughout Ayutthaya,

381
00:31:32,080 --> 00:31:34,790
admired by many people.

382
00:31:35,720 --> 00:31:37,340
He’s also skilled at swordsmanship

383
00:31:37,340 --> 00:31:38,610
and horseback riding.

384
00:31:40,680 --> 00:31:43,660
When it comes to horse riding, I’m confident.

385
00:31:44,300 --> 00:31:45,480
I even won a gold medal.

386
00:31:45,950 --> 00:31:47,900
But you can’t ride horses, my lord.

387
00:31:48,350 --> 00:31:49,610
I can.

388
00:31:50,100 --> 00:31:51,460
I’ve been riding since I was a kid.

389
00:31:51,900 --> 00:31:54,010
Have you really lost your mind?

390
00:31:54,570 --> 00:31:56,590
Did you forget you fell off a horse

391
00:31:57,280 --> 00:31:59,280
and became terrified of them?

392
00:32:02,610 --> 00:32:04,680
Maybe Gaew really changed.

393
00:32:05,390 --> 00:32:08,780
This new Gaew behaves much better than before.

394
00:32:09,720 --> 00:32:11,320
You should be happy, Dech.

395
00:32:11,770 --> 00:32:13,770
Don’t stay hung up on the old Gaew.

396
00:32:14,780 --> 00:32:16,280
He keeps talking about the past.

397
00:32:17,520 --> 00:32:19,060
And don’t move on.

398
00:32:20,570 --> 00:32:21,410
There.

399
00:32:21,410 --> 00:32:23,640
Another strange word.

400
00:32:25,040 --> 00:32:27,280
What’s moo on?

401
00:32:27,840 --> 00:32:29,190
Move on.

402
00:32:29,920 --> 00:32:31,460
Move on means

403
00:32:32,120 --> 00:32:36,550
leaving one place and going somewhere else.

404
00:32:36,990 --> 00:32:39,190
But if you don’t move on,

405
00:32:39,880 --> 00:32:43,660
you stay stuck in the past, refusing to move forward.

406
00:32:45,190 --> 00:32:47,460
Then I’ll move on first.

407
00:32:48,880 --> 00:32:50,080
You can keep talking.

408
00:33:27,980 --> 00:33:29,550
I’ll get you to your room.

409
00:33:31,460 --> 00:33:32,660
Get up.

410
00:33:33,320 --> 00:33:34,590
Ouch, P’Muen.

411
00:33:43,370 --> 00:33:44,460
You’re so heavy.

412
00:33:44,880 --> 00:33:46,900
Don’t put all your weight on me.

413
00:33:49,180 --> 00:33:51,180
P’Muen, get on the bed.

414
00:33:56,920 --> 00:33:57,680
P’Muen.

415
00:34:00,170 --> 00:34:01,170
Let me go.

416
00:34:20,100 --> 00:34:21,550
Stay here.

417
00:34:22,060 --> 00:34:23,659
Don’t go.

418
00:34:54,190 --> 00:34:55,150
P’Muen?

419
00:34:57,550 --> 00:34:58,520
P’Muen.

420
00:35:04,770 --> 00:35:05,790
P’Muen.

421
00:35:06,640 --> 00:35:07,680
P’Muen?

422
00:35:10,210 --> 00:35:11,260
P’Muen?

423
00:35:50,880 --> 00:35:52,060
Yam.

424
00:35:52,060 --> 00:35:52,990
Wake up.

425
00:35:54,060 --> 00:35:55,300
My lord.

426
00:35:55,950 --> 00:35:57,100
My lord.

427
00:35:57,720 --> 00:35:58,840
My lord.

428
00:35:59,720 --> 00:36:02,750
Please don’t ask me to sink lord Muen’s boat.

429
00:36:02,750 --> 00:36:04,390
I’m scared.

430
00:36:06,320 --> 00:36:07,550
I’m scared.

431
00:36:10,860 --> 00:36:12,550
You sank his boat?

432
00:36:13,520 --> 00:36:15,220
You sank lord Muen’s boat?

433
00:36:15,220 --> 00:36:16,120
Yam!

434
00:36:47,770 --> 00:36:49,100
-Hey!
-Hey!

435
00:36:49,100 --> 00:36:50,180
What's this?

436
00:36:50,550 --> 00:36:51,640
How would I know?

437
00:36:54,190 --> 00:36:55,100
Ow.

438
00:36:55,750 --> 00:36:56,950
Why’d you kick me?

439
00:36:57,300 --> 00:36:59,100
Why are you in my arms?

440
00:36:59,700 --> 00:37:01,500
You hugged me first,

441
00:37:01,500 --> 00:37:03,100
as if scared I’d disappear.

442
00:37:03,500 --> 00:37:05,380
And now you’re blaming me?

443
00:37:06,080 --> 00:37:07,380
Me? Hugging you?

444
00:37:07,990 --> 00:37:08,900
Yes!

445
00:37:57,170 --> 00:37:58,140
P’Muen

446
00:37:58,970 --> 00:38:00,010
P’Muen!

447
00:38:01,970 --> 00:38:02,880
P’Muen.

448
00:38:05,950 --> 00:38:06,920
What is it?

449
00:38:06,920 --> 00:38:08,100
Where are you going?

450
00:38:09,260 --> 00:38:10,900
Not your business.

451
00:38:12,150 --> 00:38:13,210
Can I come with you?

452
00:38:14,950 --> 00:38:16,210
For what?

453
00:38:16,750 --> 00:38:19,040
I’m bored being at home all day.

454
00:38:19,040 --> 00:38:20,920
I want to go to the city.

455
00:38:21,300 --> 00:38:22,340
Please let me tag along.

456
00:38:23,440 --> 00:38:24,340
Please, P’Muen.

457
00:38:26,390 --> 00:38:28,860
There are other boats. Have Yam take you.

458
00:38:30,260 --> 00:38:32,370
Don’t be so cold.

459
00:38:32,370 --> 00:38:34,150
I just want to tag along.

460
00:38:35,140 --> 00:38:36,820
I promise I won’t cause any trouble.

461
00:38:37,520 --> 00:38:38,640
Please, P’Muen.

462
00:38:39,460 --> 00:38:40,300
Please.

463
00:38:40,880 --> 00:38:42,920
Please let me come.

464
00:38:43,440 --> 00:38:45,210
Pretty please?

465
00:38:49,990 --> 00:38:50,820
Fine.

466
00:38:51,390 --> 00:38:52,320
Suit yourself.

467
00:38:53,320 --> 00:38:54,320
Thank you.

468
00:38:57,060 --> 00:38:58,740
Why are you blocking my way?

469
00:38:59,170 --> 00:39:00,640
Why are you following us?

470
00:39:00,900 --> 00:39:02,260
That’s up to my master.

471
00:39:03,750 --> 00:39:05,260
Are you challenging me?

472
00:39:05,920 --> 00:39:07,260
What challenge?

473
00:39:11,260 --> 00:39:12,260
We’ll see.

474
00:39:14,300 --> 00:39:15,300
Move.

475
00:39:15,990 --> 00:39:16,970
Get out of the way.

476
00:39:30,460 --> 00:39:31,520
P’Muen!

477
00:39:31,820 --> 00:39:32,700
P’Muen.

478
00:39:32,970 --> 00:39:33,820
P’Muen.

479
00:39:34,320 --> 00:39:35,460
What’s that?

480
00:39:40,990 --> 00:39:42,190
Wat Phanan Choeng.

481
00:39:43,060 --> 00:39:44,170
You don’t know?

482
00:39:46,170 --> 00:39:47,680
Oh.

483
00:39:47,990 --> 00:39:49,520
Wat Phanan Choeng.

484
00:39:49,520 --> 00:39:50,620
I know it.

485
00:39:51,700 --> 00:39:53,750
It’s breathtakingly beautiful.

486
00:39:55,810 --> 00:39:58,500
I have business with Reung at the police department.

487
00:39:58,860 --> 00:40:00,060
Wait for me here.

488
00:40:00,500 --> 00:40:02,370
Can I borrow your boat?

489
00:40:03,010 --> 00:40:04,550
I want to go to Wat Phanan Choeng.

490
00:40:04,920 --> 00:40:07,260
Okay? I’ll be right back.

491
00:40:07,610 --> 00:40:08,260
Gaew.

492
00:40:08,260 --> 00:40:09,500
-Let’s go, P’Yam.
-Yes, sir.

493
00:40:09,500 --> 00:40:10,440
Gaew!

494
00:40:13,340 --> 00:40:14,300
Gaew.

495
00:40:14,660 --> 00:40:15,410
Yay!

496
00:40:15,410 --> 00:40:16,770
Be careful, Gaew.

497
00:40:21,740 --> 00:40:22,520
Hey.

498
00:40:25,970 --> 00:40:27,390
How are you, my friend?

499
00:40:30,390 --> 00:40:31,810
Excuse me.

500
00:40:32,500 --> 00:40:33,610
My stomach hurts.

501
00:40:35,010 --> 00:40:36,860
I need to excuse myself to take a dump.

502
00:40:37,810 --> 00:40:38,520
Mhm.

503
00:40:50,170 --> 00:40:51,500
Hey.

504
00:40:51,500 --> 00:40:53,060
P’Yam, what’s wrong with the boat?

505
00:40:54,420 --> 00:40:56,460
Ah! My lord!

506
00:40:57,840 --> 00:41:00,060
Hey! Pin!

507
00:41:00,480 --> 00:41:02,010
Hey.

508
00:41:03,860 --> 00:41:06,420
Ah!

509
00:41:11,770 --> 00:41:13,040
Lord Gaew!

510
00:41:14,410 --> 00:41:15,440
My lord.

511
00:41:19,520 --> 00:41:20,380
Lord Muen.

512
00:41:20,380 --> 00:41:22,950
The guy who came with you fell into the water!

513
00:41:23,550 --> 00:41:24,410
Gaew.

514
00:41:27,280 --> 00:41:28,760
My lord.

515
00:41:29,320 --> 00:41:30,900
Gaew!

516
00:41:36,080 --> 00:41:37,100
Lord Muen!

517
00:41:43,060 --> 00:41:45,240
My lord, lord Muen went underwater.

518
00:42:24,280 --> 00:42:25,190
Come on, P’Muen.

519
00:42:31,370 --> 00:42:32,300
P’Muen.

520
00:42:38,280 --> 00:42:40,100
P’Muen.

521
00:42:40,100 --> 00:42:41,700
-Lord Muen.
-Pin!

522
00:42:41,700 --> 00:42:42,350
Lord Muen.

523
00:42:42,350 --> 00:42:43,080
Pin!

524
00:42:43,080 --> 00:42:44,580
You sank Lord Gaew’s boat!

525
00:42:44,580 --> 00:42:46,660
Your master tried to sink lord Muen’s boat first.

526
00:42:46,660 --> 00:42:47,480
You!

527
00:42:47,920 --> 00:42:49,240
You wanna punch me?

528
00:42:50,260 --> 00:42:51,860
Stop, P'Pin, P'Yam!

529
00:42:52,660 --> 00:42:53,950
Let's help P’Muen first.

530
00:42:55,570 --> 00:42:56,840
How?

531
00:43:09,320 --> 00:43:10,300
Huh?

532
00:43:16,040 --> 00:43:17,350
P’Muen.

533
00:43:46,500 --> 00:43:47,350
P’Muen.

534
00:43:58,170 --> 00:43:59,060
Gaew.

535
00:44:01,080 --> 00:44:02,610
You’re safe now.

536
00:44:38,950 --> 00:44:41,370
Don’t look. Don’t look at his lips.

537
00:44:41,700 --> 00:44:43,950
Don’t look. Don’t look at his lips.

538
00:44:43,950 --> 00:44:44,840
Ah.

539
00:44:47,920 --> 00:44:50,300
I want to thank you

540
00:44:51,240 --> 00:44:52,370
for saving my life.

541
00:44:57,480 --> 00:44:59,190
I should thank you too.

542
00:45:00,100 --> 00:45:01,810
You jumped in to save me,

543
00:45:01,810 --> 00:45:03,590
even though you’re not a strong swimmer.

544
00:45:04,880 --> 00:45:06,500
I helped because I wanted to.

545
00:45:07,860 --> 00:45:09,500
I also helped because I wanted to.

546
00:45:11,300 --> 00:45:13,300
As for the mouth thing…

547
00:45:13,550 --> 00:45:14,680
I know.

548
00:45:15,610 --> 00:45:18,920
I’ve seen missionaries did it to save people.

549
00:45:29,700 --> 00:45:31,900
It’s called CPR.

550
00:45:37,080 --> 00:45:38,280
CPR.

551
00:45:40,860 --> 00:45:43,480
I hope you don’t think too much about it.

552
00:45:46,790 --> 00:45:48,460
About what, P’Muen?

553
00:45:49,520 --> 00:45:51,920
I was saving a life.

554
00:45:54,260 --> 00:45:54,920
Mhm.

555
00:45:55,900 --> 00:45:57,320
If you’re not bothered …

556
00:45:57,920 --> 00:45:58,770
that’s good.

557
00:46:04,720 --> 00:46:05,840
Look over there.

558
00:46:06,770 --> 00:46:08,060
So many stars tonight.

559
00:46:14,950 --> 00:46:16,370
Where I live…

560
00:46:20,840 --> 00:46:22,520
I mean the city I live in…

561
00:46:23,950 --> 00:46:25,410
has so much light,

562
00:46:26,840 --> 00:46:28,680
so we never see this many stars.

563
00:46:32,440 --> 00:46:34,040
But you’ve lived here.

564
00:46:35,720 --> 00:46:37,100
You’re talking strangely.

565
00:46:45,880 --> 00:46:46,990
Look, P'Muen.

566
00:46:47,210 --> 00:46:47,920
Hm?

567
00:46:49,040 --> 00:46:50,010
That one.

568
00:46:50,540 --> 00:46:52,540
That's the Orion constellation.

569
00:46:52,540 --> 00:46:53,480
Which one?

570
00:46:58,370 --> 00:46:59,320
And that one,

571
00:47:00,610 --> 00:47:02,080
is the Scorpius constellation.

572
00:47:03,240 --> 00:47:04,610
And over there,

573
00:47:06,300 --> 00:47:07,950
the ones that lined up,

574
00:47:09,320 --> 00:47:11,150
is the Gemini constellation.

575
00:47:13,660 --> 00:47:15,120
I never thought

576
00:47:17,040 --> 00:47:18,520
they had names

577
00:47:19,260 --> 00:47:20,700
and shapes too.

578
00:47:22,880 --> 00:47:24,970
They’ve always been there.

579
00:47:26,440 --> 00:47:27,660
We just…

580
00:47:29,040 --> 00:47:31,280
didn’t look up to see them.

581
00:47:39,460 --> 00:47:40,640
The stars…

582
00:47:41,480 --> 00:47:43,080
are beautiful tonight.

583
00:48:01,570 --> 00:48:02,640
Maybe

584
00:48:03,170 --> 00:48:05,440
the spell really makes you lose your mind.

585
00:48:08,440 --> 00:48:09,460
Did I lose my mind?

586
00:48:11,980 --> 00:48:14,210
I wouldn’t call you crazy.

587
00:48:15,480 --> 00:48:17,320
I think you’re…

588
00:48:17,320 --> 00:48:18,590
cuter now?

589
00:48:20,900 --> 00:48:22,410
Annoying, actually.

590
00:48:42,680 --> 00:48:43,750
Aha!

591
00:49:14,410 --> 00:49:16,040
I miss grandma so much.

592
00:49:36,480 --> 00:49:37,320
My lord.

593
00:49:37,570 --> 00:49:38,610
My lord.

594
00:49:43,720 --> 00:49:44,810
You know what, P’Yam?

595
00:49:44,810 --> 00:49:45,920
Besides markets,

596
00:49:45,920 --> 00:49:48,720
my hometown also has convenience stores.

597
00:49:49,410 --> 00:49:52,300
What’s a convenience store?

598
00:49:52,770 --> 00:49:54,280
Does it sell magical things?

599
00:49:54,680 --> 00:49:56,300
It’s just a normal store

600
00:49:56,700 --> 00:49:59,080
that opens all day and all night.

601
00:49:59,790 --> 00:50:01,300
How’s that possible?

602
00:50:01,300 --> 00:50:02,640
People need sleep.

603
00:50:03,080 --> 00:50:04,860
Are there a hundred servants working?

604
00:50:04,860 --> 00:50:05,970
No.

605
00:50:05,970 --> 00:50:07,900
The staff just work in shifts.

606
00:50:07,900 --> 00:50:09,300
No hundred servants.

607
00:50:12,550 --> 00:50:13,420
Wow.

608
00:50:27,770 --> 00:50:28,790
You can put it here.

609
00:50:34,300 --> 00:50:35,300
Thank you.

610
00:50:40,920 --> 00:50:41,790
Help!

611
00:50:42,410 --> 00:50:43,260
Help!

612
00:50:44,170 --> 00:50:45,080
My lord.

613
00:50:55,640 --> 00:50:57,210
Argh!

614
00:51:05,860 --> 00:51:07,440
Officer, over there!

615
00:51:07,440 --> 00:51:08,680
That way.

616
00:51:15,680 --> 00:51:16,480
Here.

617
00:51:18,860 --> 00:51:20,100
Thank you so much.

618
00:51:20,640 --> 00:51:22,190
If it weren’t for you, I’d be in trouble.

619
00:51:23,990 --> 00:51:25,570
Your accent is so good.

620
00:51:27,720 --> 00:51:29,640
I’ve lived here since I was born.

621
00:51:31,990 --> 00:51:34,420
My name is Maria Guyomar.

622
00:51:35,610 --> 00:51:37,970
And you?

623
00:51:39,440 --> 00:51:41,540
Maria Guyomar.

624
00:51:45,440 --> 00:51:47,610
12 Thai Desserts.

625
00:51:47,610 --> 00:51:49,360
By Thao Thong Kip Ma.

626
00:51:50,550 --> 00:51:51,590
Who is that?

627
00:51:51,590 --> 00:51:52,620
What a funny name.

628
00:51:53,040 --> 00:51:53,700
Hey.

629
00:51:53,700 --> 00:51:55,080
Don’t make fun of her.

630
00:51:55,080 --> 00:51:57,210
She was the head of the royal dessert kitchen

631
00:51:57,210 --> 00:51:58,410
for King Narai.

632
00:52:00,320 --> 00:52:01,280
So?

633
00:52:02,240 --> 00:52:03,370
What’s your name?

634
00:52:04,150 --> 00:52:05,660
My name is... Great.

635
00:52:06,350 --> 00:52:06,970
No.

636
00:52:07,500 --> 00:52:08,410
It's Gaew.

637
00:52:09,790 --> 00:52:10,620
Gaew.

638
00:52:11,880 --> 00:52:13,300
Thank you again.

639
00:52:16,840 --> 00:52:19,240
Maria Guyomar.

640
00:52:20,170 --> 00:52:21,640
You can call me Mali.

641
00:53:56,620 --> 00:53:57,970
I’m a new person now.

642
00:53:57,970 --> 00:53:59,650
I apologize for what I did in the past.

643
00:54:01,530 --> 00:54:04,040
Why are we secretly following Lord Gaew?

644
00:54:04,040 --> 00:54:05,900
I’m afraid he’s going to cause trouble.

645
00:54:09,060 --> 00:54:11,060
You can call me Falcon.

646
00:54:15,360 --> 00:54:16,670
What’s happening to me?

647
00:54:16,970 --> 00:54:19,390
Why is my heart racing like this?

648
00:54:20,750 --> 00:54:21,690
Why are you arresting me?

649
00:54:21,690 --> 00:54:24,300
You’re a murder suspect.

650
00:54:24,300 --> 00:54:25,760
Me? A murderer?
